  - name: string
  - enabled: boolean
  - cronExpression: string
  - timezone: string
  - targetContentId: string
  - inputPayload: any
  - permissions: 'suggest-only'|'approval-required'|'conditional-auto'|'bounded-autopilot'
  - constraints: { maxActions?: number; spendLimit?: number; allowedTools?: string[] }
  - safetyRails: string[]
  - retryPolicy: { backoffMs: number; maxRetries: number; deadLetterQueue?: string }
  - createdAt/updatedAt
- MemoryScope
  - id: string
  - contentItemId: string
  - scopeName: string
  - dataBlob: any
  - ttlSeconds: number
  - accessControls: any
  - createdAt/updatedAt
- RunArtifact
  - id: string
  - contentItemId: string
  - runId: string
  - type: 'diff'|'generatedContent'|'log'|'artifact'
  - path: string
  - signedUrl: string
  - retentionPolicy: string
  - createdAt
- AuditLog
  - id: string
  - contentItemId: string
  - action: string
  - actorId: string
  - timestamp: string
  - details: any
- PlatformPublishRecord
  - id: string
  - contentItemId: string
  - platform: string
  - status: 'queued'|'in-progress'|'completed'|'failed'
  - scheduledAt: string
  - startedAt: string
  - finishedAt: string
  - logs: string

API Endpoints (example set):
- GET /api/content
- POST /api/content
- GET /api/content/:id
- PUT /api/content/:id
- DELETE /api/content/:id
- POST /api/content/:id/versions
- GET /api/content/:id/versions
- POST /api/content/:id/publish
- GET /api/content/:id/memory
- POST /api/content/:id/memory
- GET /api/content/:id/artifacts
- GET /api/content/:id/audit
- POST /api/schedules
- GET /api/schedules/:id/run

Security:
- Auth: JWT/OAuth2; enforce RBAC: roles like Editor, Approver, Admin.
- Access controls on MemoryScope and content actions; scoped memory cannot be accessed outside allowed contexts.
- All mutations require proper validation and permission checks.
- Signed URLs for artifacts with short lifetimes; retention policies enforced at the storage layer.

Validation:
- All API responses validated; use data?.field or defaults; guard arrays with (array ?? []) or Array.isArray(array) ? array.map(...) : [].
- On frontend data loading: const items = data ?? [] ; Array.isArray(items) guard usage.

Validation Rules:
- Inputs: title must be non-empty; content length >= 1; schedule cron expression validated; time zone valid; platform list non-empty if publishing toggled on.
- Versioning: every save creates a new ContentVersion; currentVersionId must reference an existing version.
- Memory: TTL > 0 when set; accessControls not empty for restricted scopes.
- Artifacts: path and signedUrl must be non-empty when created.

Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Create Content editor loads with a draft or empty state and autosaves without errors; data is guarded against null values (no runtime crashes).
- [ ] AI-assisted drafting prompts populate accurately; research pane shows relevant citations with ability to add inline notes; all array-like data is guarded using (data ?? []) or Array.isArray checks.
- [ ] Versioning works: create version, view diffs, compare view, and restore to previous version without data loss; correct diffs displayed.
- [ ] Scheduling supports per-platform toggles, time zones, and recurrence; scheduled runs execute and publish to platforms; run logs are captured.
- [ ] Memory API correctly reads/writes scoped memory with TTL and access controls; no unauthorized reads.
- [ ] Artifacts are stored securely with signed URLs and retention policies; downloads succeed and expire correctly.
- [ ] Content Library integration: Create Content can be opened from library, edited, and saved back with versioning and artifacts updated.
- [ ] Access controls enforced: unauthorized actions are blocked; audit trail captures all actions.

UI/UX Guidelines
- Apply LifeOps design system:
  - Card-based modular layout with 12-column grid and 24–32px gutters.
  - Sidebar navigation with active state indicators; top bar with search and quick actions.
  - Dark background, high-contrast typography, and accent colors from the palette.
  - Interactive elements: rounded buttons, large input fields with soft borders, focus outlines in accent color.
  - Accessibility: keyboard navigable, aria-labels, screen-reader friendly.

Visual Style
- As provided: deep charcoal surfaces, flat color blocks, neon accents for charts if used, but primarily flat UI with depth via elevation.
- Use the exact palette tokens wherever possible:
  - Primary background: #18191C
  - Card surfaces: #232429 or #1F2124
  - Accent: #4F8CFF
  - Success: #5ED36D
  - Warning/Info: #FFD66C
  - Error: #EF6464
  - Text: #FFFFFF (headings), #AEB2B8 (secondary), #74777D (placeholders)
  - Borders: rgba(38,40,44,0.3) to rgba(38,40,44,0.6)

Mandatory Coding Standards — Runtime Safety
- Supabase-like results handling:
  - const items = data ?? [];
- Array methods:
  - (items ?? []).map(...)
  - Array.isArray(items) ? items.map(...) : []
- useState defaults for arrays:
  - const [items, setItems] = useState<Type[]>([]);
- API response shapes:
  - const list = Array.isArray(response?.data) ? response.data : [];
- Optional chaining:
  - obj?.property?.nested
- Destructuring with defaults:
  - const { items = [], count = 0 } = response ?? {};

Development Prompts for AI Tool
- Generate a fully-typed React + TypeScript frontend module for Create Content that includes:
  - Editor area with markdown support, collaboration cursors, autosave, and connectable to Content Pipeline for drafting prompts.
  - AI Assistant sidebar with sections for Outline, Ideas, and Rewrites; each section should fetch prompts and maintain local state with safe guards.
  - ResearchPane showing citations and source metadata with relevance scores; allow tagging/categorization.
  - Versioning/DiffViewer that fetches ContentVersion history and renders diffs with a side-by-side view.
  - SchedulingPanel that validates cron or UI-based scheduling, handles time zone, and supports multiple platforms with platform toggles.
  - MemoryInspector and MemoryBridge implementing scoped memory read/write with TTL and ACLs; safely handle nulls.
  - ArtifactsStoragePanel to display artifacts with signed URLs and retention status; implement safe rendering for possibly empty lists.
  - ContentLibraryList to browse and filter content items; ensure guard clauses on list rendering.
  - AuditTrailPanel to display action logs and inter-agent communications; ensure privacy controls.
- Implement data models and API hooks:
  - TypeScript interfaces for ContentItem, ContentVersion, Schedule, MemoryScope, RunArtifact, AuditLog, PlatformPublishRecord.
  - Custom React hooks for data fetching with null-safe handling: useQueryContent, useContentVersions, useMemoryScoper, useArtifacts, useSchedules, etc.
  - API client wrappers with proper payload validation and response guards.
- State management:
  - Use React Query or SWR for data fetching; use useState/useEffect for local UI state with proper initialization (e.g., [] defaults).
  - Ensure mutation hooks validate input and enforce optimistic updates with rollback on error.
- Security and permissions:
  - Guard all mutations with authorization checks; memory read/write respects scope ACLs.
  - Include audit trail capture for UI actions; ensure sensitive fields are redacted when displayed.
- Accessibility:
  - aria-labels, keyboard shortcuts for common actions, and proper focus management.
- Testing:
  - Unit tests for data transformers and reducers; integration tests for memory read/write flows; e2e tests for create/edit/publish flows.

Notes and Assumptions
- The prompt should be capable of generating a complete, production-ready module with the above components.
- If certain features require placeholder implementations (e.g., collaboration cursors or external AI calls), provide clear stubs with extensible interfaces and default behavior that satisfies runtime safety and UI expectations.
- Do not assume an external API is available; design with clear extension points for internal services (Content Pipeline, Vector DB, Storage).

This prompt is ready to be consumed by an AI development tool to produce a complete, end-to-end Create Content feature set that adheres to the project’s architectural patterns, UI guidelines, and runtime safety requirements.

